1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:02,784
What if money actually grew on trees?

2
00:00:07,650 --> 00:00:09,571
At first, everyone would think

3
00:00:09,791 --> 00:00:11,218
they had just become rich.

4
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:17,294
Then every tree on Earth

5
00:00:17,514 --> 00:00:19,365
starts producing cash.

6
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:26,282
Suddenly, almost everyone has more money

7
00:00:26,502 --> 00:00:27,981
than they can spend.

8
00:00:31,650 --> 00:00:33,122
But there is one problem.

9
00:00:33,342 --> 00:00:35,450
More money does not mean more food,

10
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:37,534
houses, or resources.

11
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:41,561
As cash becomes unlimited,

12
00:00:41,781 --> 00:00:44,147
prices could rise faster and faster.

13
00:00:47,650 --> 00:00:50,172
Eventually, those piles of money

14
00:00:50,392 --> 00:00:52,176
might barely buy anything.

15
00:00:55,650 --> 00:00:57,958
Because real wealth is not just money.

16
00:00:58,178 --> 00:01:00,634
It is the things people can actually produce.

17
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:06,553
The richest person in this world

18
00:01:06,773 --> 00:01:08,983
might still be unable to buy dinner.

19
00:01:12,650 --> 00:01:14,804
Would you still want money to grow on trees?

20
00:01:15,024 --> 00:01:16,511
Tell us: yes or no?
